# Worked example (RECIPES.md, "A new prop from two disc textures"): a winged Toad head, a shop sign
# made of Toad's head (c_kinopio, image 8) and a Paragoomba's wing (c_kuribo, image 5, its first
# wing), the wing twice, once flipped. An example: the game doesn't load it.

image examples/winged_cap.png
  canvas 112 64
  # Toad's head (120x112) at half size, keeping the game's texel look
  piece head model c_kinopio 8
  @head scale 60 56 texel
  # the wing: the sheet's first wing (32 texels wide) at three quarters; the other side is the same
  # wing flipped
  piece left model c_kuribo 5
  @left crop 0 0 32 64
  @left scale 24 48 texel
  piece right model c_kuribo 5
  @right crop 0 0 32 64
  @right scale 24 48 texel
  @right flip x
  # the wings first, tipped up behind the cap; the head over their roots
  paste left 6 0
  paste right 82 0
  paste head 26 6
end
